  "note": "Election of the rural district council by proportional representation, 1920 (polled 5 June 1920). Only the Lurgan end of the district was found; the other electoral area(s) are not filed. First preferences only (the transfers are not printed). The \"three members of the Rural Council to which this end of the district is entitled\", elected by proportional representation; the Lurgan Mail does not name the electoral area. Valid poll 1,331, spoilt 86, quota 333. Campbell reached the quota on the fifth count; Faloon and Ruddell were declared elected on the seventh count without reaching it. Counted at Lurgan Workhouse on Monday 7 June 1920 by W. J. Corner, returning officer. The Northern Whig says nine candidates were nominated for the three seats."
